SUMMARY:📸 Sunset on the beach
DESCRIPTION:The beach in front of the hotel faces west\, so the sun sets ri
 ght over the water.\n\n🕘 Hours: Public beach\, open all day\; sunset ab
 out 17:33 on 1/6\n🚶 Getting there: about 3 min walk from Villa Del Sol 
 Boutique Hotel\n\n📍 Playas del Coco Beach\, Guanacaste\, Playa del Coco
 \, El Coco\, Sardinal\, Guanacaste\n🧭 https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?
 api=1&destination=Playas%20del%20Coco%20Beach%2C%20Guanacaste
LOCATION:Playas del Coco Beach\, Guanacaste\, Playa del Coco\, El Coco\, Sa
 rdinal\, Guanacaste
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=Playas%20del%20Coco%
 20Beach%2C%20Guanacaste
GEO:10.5585;-85.6915
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS="Playa del Coco, El Coco, S
 ardinal, Guanacaste";X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE="Playas del Coco Beach, Gu
 anacaste":geo:10.5585,-85.6915
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:costa-rica-2027-jan-6-11-d1-5@travel-plan
DTSTAMP:20261119T234308Z
DTSTART:20270107T010000Z
DTEND:20270107T020000Z
SUMMARY:🍽️ Seafood by the sea
DESCRIPTION:Walk into Coco town (about 15 minutes): Papagayo Seafood (often
  live music) or Mar Azul\; take a taxi back if you don’t feel like walki
 ng.\n\n🚗 Getting there: about 3 min drive from Playas del Coco Beach (~
 1.7 km\, estimated)\n\n📍 Playas del Coco\, Guanacaste\, Costa Rica\, Pl
 ayas del Coco\, Sardinal\, Carrillo\, Guanacaste\n🧭 https://www.google.
 com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=Playas%20del%20Coco%2C%20Guanacaste%2C%20C
 osta%20Rica
LOCATION:Playas del Coco\, Guanacaste\, Costa Rica\, Playas del Coco\, Sard
 inal\, Carrillo\, Guanacaste
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=Playas%20del%20Coco%
 2C%20Guanacaste%2C%20Costa%20Rica
GEO:10.5505;-85.6995
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS="Playas del Coco, Sardinal,
  Carrillo, Guanacaste";X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE="Playas del Coco, Guanac
 aste, Costa Rica":geo:10.5505,-85.6995
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:costa-rica-2027-jan-6-11-d1-6@travel-plan
DTSTAMP:20261119T234308Z
DTSTART:20270107T020000Z
DTEND:20270107T030000Z
SUMMARY:📸 Stargazing on the beach
DESCRIPTION:Tomorrow\, 1/7\, is the new moon\, so tonight is nearly moonles
 s\; Guanacaste’s dry season is mostly clear and it is fully dark by 19:0
 0. The darker north end of Coco beach is right in front of the hotel\; wal
 k away from the streetlights\, lie on a towel and look: Orion is high in t
 he southeast with Sirius\, the brightest star\, below it\; after 21:00 loo
 k low in the south for Canopus (the second-brightest star\, never visible 
 from Toronto). Use Stellarium or SkyView on your phone to identify stars. 
 Bring only your phone and a towel\, no valuables\, and don’t wander far\
 ; tomorrow is an early start on mountain roads\, so don’t stay up too la
 te.\n\n🕘 Hours: Public beach\, open all day\; sunset about 17:33 on 1/6
 \n🚗 Getting there: about 3 min drive from Playas del Coco (~1.7 km\, es
 timated)\n\n📍 Playas del Coco Beach\, Guanacaste\, Playa del Coco\, El 
 Coco\, Sardinal\, Guanacaste\n🧭 https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&
 destination=Playas%20del%20Coco%20Beach%2C%20Guanacaste\nMoon phases (time
 anddate): https://www.timeanddate.com/moon/phases/costa-rica/liberia?year=
 2027
LOCATION:Playas del Coco Beach\, Guanacaste\, Playa del Coco\, El Coco\, Sa
 rdinal\, Guanacaste
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=Playas%20del%20Coco%
 20Beach%2C%20Guanacaste
GEO:10.5585;-85.6915
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS="Playa del Coco, El Coco, S
 ardinal, Guanacaste";X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE="Playas del Coco Beach, Gu
 anacaste":geo:10.5585,-85.6915
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:costa-rica-2027-jan-6-11-d2-0@travel-plan
DTSTAMP:20261119T234308Z
DTSTART:20270107T130000Z
DTEND:20270107T142000Z
SUMMARY:🚗 Check out and set off
DESCRIPTION:Bring some cash (the waterfall is cash only). South via Liberia
  and Bagaces\, about 1 h 15 min to the waterfall.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:costa-rica-2027-jan-6-11-d2-1@travel-plan
DTSTAMP:20261119T234308Z
DTSTART:20270107T142000Z
DTEND:20270107T152000Z
SUMMARY:📸 Llanos de Cortés waterfall
DESCRIPTION:About 30 concrete steps with a rope handrail\; sandy at the bot
 tom\, rocky at the edge and in the water. You can take a dip\; watch your 
 step on the rocks so you don't roll an ankle.\n\n🕘 Hours: Daily 8:00–
 16:00 (last entry about 15:30)\; ₡4\,000 per person\, cash only\n🚗 Ge
 tting there: about 80 min drive from Villa Del Sol Boutique Hotel (64 km)\
 n\n📍 Llanos de Cortés Waterfall\, Bagaces\, Ruta 1\, 7 km al noroeste 
 de Bagaces\, Guanacaste\n🧭 https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&desti
 nation=Llanos%20de%20Cort%C3%A9s%20Waterfall%2C%20Bagaces
LOCATION:Llanos de Cortés Waterfall\, Bagaces\, Ruta 1\, 7 km al noroeste 
 de Bagaces\, Guanacaste
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=Llanos%20de%20Cort%C
 3%A9s%20Waterfall%2C%20Bagaces
GEO:10.524302;-85.298602
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS="Ruta 1, 7 km al noroeste d
 e Bagaces, Guanacaste";X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE="Llanos de Cortés Water
 fall, Bagaces":geo:10.524302,-85.298602
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:costa-rica-2027-jan-6-11-d2-2@travel-plan
DTSTAMP:20261119T234308Z
DTSTART:20270107T152000Z
DTEND:20270107T190000Z
SUMMARY:🚗 Route 1 to Monteverde
DESCRIPTION:Via Cañas\, turning onto Route 606 for the climb\, about 2.5 h
 ours\; Route 606 is paved but steep with tight bends\, so take it slowly. 
 Reach Santa Elena around 12:00 for a quick lunch.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:costa-rica-2027-jan-6-11-d2-3@travel-plan
DTSTAMP:20261119T234308Z
DTSTART:20270107T190000Z
DTEND:20270107T220000Z
SUMMARY:🎟️ 100% Aventura ziplines
DESCRIPTION:About 2.5–3 hours: 10 ziplines\, the longest 1\,590 m\, the l
 ongest in Costa Rica\; the last two are Superman lines you fly face-down\,
  plus one Tarzan swing (optional). From USD72 per person on the official s
 ite (plus tax)\, transport not included\; about 10 minutes’ drive from t
 own. Check the booking page for slots (commonly 8:00\, 11:00\, 13:00\, 15:
 00). Her Achilles is still in rehab: on the Superman lines staff brake you
  and help you stand\, so the stop itself is gentle\; what to watch is the 
 stairs and forest paths between platforms\, and the occasional foot touchd
 own at the end of the regular lines\, so ask her physio before booking.\n\
 n🕘 Hours: Zipline tours leave daily at 8:00\, 11:00 and 14:00\, about 3
  h (some listings also show 13:00 and 15:00\; go by your booking)\n🚗 Ge
 tting there: about 145 min drive from Llanos de Cortés Waterfall (108 km)
 \n\n📍 100% Aventura Zipline\, Monteverde\, Camino a la Reserva Santa El
 ena\, Monteverde\, Puntarenas\n🧭 https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1
 &destination=100%25%20Aventura%20Zipline%2C%20Monteverde\nBook 100% Aventu
 ra (official): https://fareharbor.com/embeds/book/aventuracanopytour/items
 /39178/calendar/?ref=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.aventuracanopytour.com&language=en-
 us\n100% Aventura official site: https://www.aventuracanopytour.com/\nAlte
 rnative: Selvatura ziplines (also has a Superman line): https://selvatura.
 com/packages/
LOCATION:100% Aventura Zipline\, Monteverde\, Camino a la Reserva Santa Ele
 na\, Monteverde\, Puntarenas
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=100%25%20Aventura%20
 Zipline%2C%20Monteverde
GEO:10.3388806;-84.8241529
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS="Camino a la Reserva Santa 
 Elena, Monteverde, Puntarenas";X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE="100% Aventura Z
 ipline, Monteverde":geo:10.3388806,-84.8241529
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
